WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.820
It seems like a lot of movies have been shot
in London lately.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.690
One example is Bridget Jones’ Baby, the
latest episode from Bridget Jones saga which

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.120
I might have seen...

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:23.340
Look at those skyscrapers in the background,
those were simply not there in the first movie

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.340
of the saga.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:28.990
In fact, London´s skyline has changed dramatically
in the last 10 years.

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:33.190
And this is surprising because we are not
talking about an emerging economy like China

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:35.850
or Singapore.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.480
Actually, the overall economy in the UK has
not performed especially well in the last

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:42.520
few years.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.079
However, London is another world.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:51.070
Today it is one of the four fastest growing
capitals on the planet - growing almost at

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.449
the same level as Dubai.

00:00:53.449 --> 00:01:03.980
Their population has increased by 50% rate
in just two decades.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:07.649
This is particularly odd in a continent like
Europe, where all the countries are seeing

00:01:07.649 --> 00:01:09.390
overall population decline.

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:13.500
Instead, London has 3 million more inhabitants.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:19.240
And in the finance world, London city is now
more important than New York City itself.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:23.500
So, you might wonder what exactly happened
in this city which would explain this massive

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:24.500
success?

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:30.360
That’s what we’re looking at in today’s
Visual Politik video!

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.630
IMMIGRATION

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:35.130
United Kingdom has always been a country of
immigrants.

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:37.760
And, London was always the main destination.

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:43.250
Nonetheless, in the last decade, immigration
has absolutely skyrocketed.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:48.200
After Poland became part of European Union,
in 2004, a lot of Poles moved effortlessly

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:54.330
to the city as no visa was required.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:02:01.410
The same happened when Bulgaria and Romania
became EU members in 2007.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:07.220
This created a whole new influx of immigrants
that added those from India or Pakistan.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:11.489
These European immigrants typically have higher
education and university degrees.

00:02:11.489 --> 00:02:16.810
In fact, today London has over 1.7 million
highly skilled workers while New York has

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:18.520
just 1.6 million.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:24.420
Immigrants are not only working the jobs Brits
don’t want to do anymore, but they are also

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:28.130
starting businesses and getting hired by high
tech companies.

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:39.200
But 

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:44.260
companies are far more than just job creating
machines, or factors that boost economic growth.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:48.360
The fact that London has more well educated
people means more bars, more exhibitions,

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.360
more culture…

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:52.210
In summary, all the things that make a city
look “cool”.

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:56.440
As an example: Where is the best Peruvian
restaurant outside of Peru?

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:01.831
Well, according to all the gastronomical guides,
it is CEVICHE, and of course, it´s in the

00:03:01.831 --> 00:03:08.930
British capital.

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:14.530
And this is how London created a virtuous
circle that attracted more and more people.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:19.819
This is why, in 2008, after the financial
crisis, many Spaniards, Portuguese and Italians

00:03:19.819 --> 00:03:24.390
who wanted to leave their countries, saw London
as the main destination.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:26.420
It was more than just a good place to find
a job.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.120
It was a cool place to live.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:32.200
This is what economists call the “NETWORK
EFFECT”.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:36.470
The more people and the more companies you
have, the easier it is to attract highly skilled

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:38.720
immigrants.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:52.740
For a better understanding, since 2010, over
1000 startups have been created In London

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:54.530
every single year.

00:03:54.530 --> 00:04:00.640
But hold on a minute because there is more!

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.110
THE CITY OF LONDON

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:08.110
All the skyscrapers you see here are concentrated
in an small area, not bigger than a square

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:09.110
mile.

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:11.610
This place is called the “CITY OF LONDON”.

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:25.970
Yes, on the one hand, we have London, and
then, there is the City of London, which works

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:28.610
like a country of it’s own within the United
Kingdom.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:33.970
Yes, we British usually say that Great Britain
is made up of four nations: England, Wales,

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:35.730
Scotland and Northern Ireland.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:38.320
But this is not exactly true...

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:44.030
In fact, we should add a fifth one, and this
is the City of London, which has its own Mayor

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:51.690
and its own laws.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:05:02.000
London’s Mayor is the man you are watching
on the screen now, his name is SADIQ KHAN.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:08.210
But the City of London has its own Lord Mayor,
he is called JEFFREY MONTEVANS.

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:13.100
One of the characteristics of The City, AKA
the Square Mile, is that during the elections,

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:16.410
both citizens and companies have the right
to vote.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:19.440
For instance, Unilever has it’s headquarters
here in the Square Mile.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:28.020
This means that when elections are held, Unilever
can vote.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:32.000
So, you might wonder…

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.800
Does the vote of Unilever count the same as
one from a smaller company?

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.210
The answer is no.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:42.200
The number of votes a company gets will depend
on how many people they employ within THE

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:49.550
CITY.

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:56.620
By the way, the music that you are listening
to is THE FORGOTTEN VOICE, a pop-rock band

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:59.389
from Ireland who sent us their music.

00:05:59.389 --> 00:06:09.770
If you like it, you will find more information
on the description box below.

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:20.020
And now you might wondering whether the City
of London a FISCAL HAVEN?

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.620
The answer is NO.

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:24.550
All across UK, taxes are fairly similar.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:29.610
But it is true that the Square Mile has far
more business-friendly policies than anywhere

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:31.050
else in the UK.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:34.870
For instance, their urban development laws
are way more open and free than in the rest

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:37.650
of London - this is why they have more skyscrapers.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:41.710
But when it comes to taxes, they are not a
haven whatsoever.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:42.800
But hold on a minute...

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.300
The City itself does play a very important
role.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:50.010
This is because the Lord Mayor’s main task
is travelling all around the world promoting

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:53.150
London’s benefits for investment.

00:06:53.150 --> 00:07:01.540
“The Lord Mayor of the City of London, Alderman
Alan Yarrow, is to lead a business delegation

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:07.110
to Indonesia (19-21 May) helping to make sure
London and the UK remain the regional partner

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:10.800
of choice when it comes to financial and professional
services.”

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:18.550
So, in a way, you can say that London has
its own marketing department showcasing all

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:22.530
their advantages to the world!

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:25.070
BUSINESS CONCENTRATION

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:27.720
The US economy is divided among different
cities.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:33.110
For example, politics is centered in Washington
DC, finance in New York City, entertainment

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:36.850
in Los Angeles, and technology in San Francisco.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:41.720
The same happens in Germany, where you have
cities like Berlin, Frankfurt or Munich.

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:45.360
And in Spain, you have Barcelona and Madrid…

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:50.650
Britain on the other hand has London... and
just London.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:53.979
The rest of the cities are far less important
for British economy.

00:07:53.979 --> 00:07:58.900
In fact, London makes 1 out of every 5 pounds
generated in the whole country.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:04.180
In this city you will find all the major Government
institutions, the banks, the technological

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:29.600
sector, the fashion centre, etc…

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:34.560
And to this, we should add another key element:
English.

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:40.219
As you know, the UK has held pretty good relationship
with United States (at least for the last

00:08:40.219 --> 00:08:41.219
two centuries.)

00:08:41.219 --> 00:08:46.310
Even though there is no trade agreement between
the two countries, they have much history

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:51.040
in common and, most important of all, we both
speak the same language.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:59.040
Add to this the fact that United Kingdom is
(currently) a part of the European Union and

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:03.309
you can easily understand why London has become
the gateway for any American company wanting

00:09:03.309 --> 00:09:19.420
to do business 

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:25.649
in European markets.

00:09:25.649 --> 00:09:34.790
But now the big question is how will BREXIT
affect London’s growth?

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:40.519
One thing is clear: even though the majority
of the British population voted in favour

00:09:40.519 --> 00:09:44.429
of leaving the EU, Londoners wanted to REMAIN.

00:09:44.429 --> 00:09:46.869
So what do you think?

